# The firmware images this tree compiles in, and the digests they must have.
#
# One line per image: the digest, the name the driver asks for it by, and the
# blob translation unit that carries it.  The bytes are generated from the files
# the board's Linux lane ships for the same chips - the files the kernel drivers
# load; the digests below are the anchor that ties each compiled-in array back to
# its file.  The check that enforces them is
# tests/host/linuxkpi-body-test/check-firmware.sh, which can also be pointed at a
# directory holding reference copies of the images for a two-source comparison.
#
# The driver name is the one the driver requests, not the file's name on a host:
# a driver that walks format numbers downwards asks for the highest first (rtw89
# on 8851B asks for the -1 form before the bare one, fw.c:1006-1010).
2ff74315287529dec2e50eb57d6e0c97d2116f28ae166773ccdf93b6360000c4  rtl8188eufw.bin       rtl8188eufw_blob.c
1c4ccb5fa06bf5649146025e95993db66876a1fbc0bd766ec05686587f69c1b7  rtw8851b_fw-1.bin     rtw8851b_fw_blob.c
2ef409bc418549fcf294061dd0cae1fc22fd9da79b60524950b25de18732f3f0  rtw88/rtw8821c_fw.bin  rtw8821c_fw_blob.c
